## 9. Fixing "File in Editor is Not Runnable" in IntelliJ

If your IDE says the file in the editor is not runnable, it usually means IntelliJ doesn't recognize your folder as a proper Java project.

1. **Mark the source folder as Sources Root:**
   In the project file panel on the left side of your screen, locate the `src` folder. Right-click on it, hover over **Mark Directory As**, and select **Sources Root**.
2. **Ensure a Java SDK is selected:**
   Go to **File > Project Structure** (or press `Ctrl + Alt + Shift + S` on Windows / `Cmd + ;` on Mac). Check the **Project SDK** field. If it says "No SDK", click the dropdown and select your installed Java version (e.g., Java 17 or 21), then click **Apply** and **OK**.
3. **Check for the main method:**
   Open your main `.java` file and verify it contains `public static void main(String[] args)`. A green play button (**▶**) will appear in the gutter once it is fully recognized as runnable.
